&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own program delivery&lt;/strong&gt; — build and own project plans, map dependencies across teams, independently assess and mitigate risks and issues, and keep initiatives on a predictable timeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate needs into crisp requirements&lt;/strong&gt; — turn vague business, clinical, or partner requests into clear, actionable requirements and decisions that product and engineering teams can build against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run Product &amp;amp; Tech operating rhythms&lt;/strong&gt; — lead quarterly planning, goal setting, roadmap reviews, and launch readiness and communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen feedback loops&lt;/strong&gt; — own and improve alignment, communication, and processes between Product &amp;amp; Tech teams and their cross-functional counterparts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive data-informed decisions&lt;/strong&gt; — evaluate the performance and impact of major initiatives and prepare and deliver clear, concise recommendations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own core tooling&lt;/strong&gt; — determine, administer, and improve the operational tooling and systems (project trackers, documentation, dashboards) that give the org visibility and leverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finish the job&lt;/strong&gt; — ensure initiatives don&#39;t just launch, but reach long-term optimization and post-launch learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Who You Are / Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
