&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in program management, project management, or operations in a complex, cross-functional environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong program management fundamentals&lt;/strong&gt; — planning, sequencing, milestone and dependency tracking, and risk management, with exceptional attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A documentation and systems thinker&lt;/strong&gt; — you naturally reach for playbooks, templates, and repeatable processes instead of doing the same manual task 100 times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A clear communicator&lt;/strong&gt; — you give stakeholders proactive visibility into your work, run effective meetings, and capture decisions and action items so nothing falls through the cracks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and biased toward action&lt;/strong&gt; — you ask sharp questions, propose solutions rather than waiting for instructions, and know when to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with the technical side of the house&lt;/strong&gt; — you don&#39;t need to code, but product development lifecycles, integrations, APIs, and data aren&#39;t a black box to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative, with high empathy and high accountability&lt;/strong&gt; — you support your teammates, give and receive direct feedback, and hold yourself to a high bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth-minded&lt;/strong&gt; — you actively seek feedback and are excited to grow toward leading larger, more complex programs end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deeply motivated by Modern Health&#39;s mission&lt;/strong&gt; and passionate about enabling better mental health outcomes at scale&lt;/li&gt;
