&lt;p&gt;Modern Health is a fully remote workforce and a hyper-growth company that is often recognized for its excellence, winning awards such as &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/modern-health-named-to-fast-companys-annual-list-of-the-worlds-most-innovative-companies-for-2023-301761291.html&quot;&gt;World’s Most Innovative Companies&lt;/a&gt; of 2023 by Fast Company, &lt;a href=&quot;https://thebusinessreport.com/the-top-25-companies-of-san-francisco-for-2023/&quot;&gt;Top 25 Companies of San Francisco 2023&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/archetype-and-welcoa-announce-winners-of-the-2023-well-being-trailblazer-awards-301880865.html&quot;&gt;2023 Well-Being Trailblazer Award&lt;/a&gt;. To protect our culture and help our team stay connected, we require overlapping hours for everyone. While many roles may function from anywhere in the world—see individual job listing for more—US based team members who live outside the Pacific time zone are expected to work at least six hours between 8 am and 5 pm Pacific time each workday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for driven, creative, and passionate individuals to join in our mission. An inclusive and diverse culture are key components of mental well-being in the workplace, and that starts with how we build our own team. If you&#39;re excited about a role, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Talent Operations and Workplace Coordinator, you&#39;re the person who makes the hiring process feel effortless and the SF office feel like the best part of someone&#39;s day. You&#39;re the first message a candidate gets and the first face they see when they walk in for an onsite, the reason a day of back-to-back interviews lands without a hitch, and the one who notices the office needs restocking before anyone has to ask.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, in-person role, split mostly between coordinating details for our hiring process and running our office, with occasional support to the broader People Operations team. You&#39;ll be in the San Francisco office location two days a week as a baseline, with flexibility to come in more when we have interviews, on-sites meetings, or events happening.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll do well here if you like variety, don&#39;t mind switching gears a few times a day, and take real pride in the small things that make an office, and a hiring process, feel well run. Bonus points if you&#39;re already using AI in your day-to-day and are eager to find smarter, more efficient ways to run our recruiting tools and workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiting Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end interview scheduling across candidates, hiring managers, and interviewers, managing calendars, communications, and every touchpoint along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and organize all interview logistics, scheduling, confirmations, reschedules, booking team debrief meetings and more. Serve as the primary point of contact for candidates related to their interview calendar from initial screening through offer, keeping communication warm, professional, and timely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor interviewer availability and flag scheduling conflicts early to keep things moving, even across multiple time zones and calendars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Greenhouse ATS&#39;s scheduling tools to automate where you can and keep manual work to a minimum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate candidate records and interview feedback in Greenhouse ATS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support referral coordination and onboarding logistics (paperwork, system access, first-day setup)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SF Office &amp;amp; Workplace:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the office tidy, stocked, and running smoothly day to day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor relationships (cleaning, maintenance, food &amp;amp; beverage, security) and hold them to a high standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run in-office events, team lunches, and celebrations, including catering setup and takedown&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage office access including badge distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host guests, candidates, and visitors so every visit reflects well on the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support space planning, furniture moves, and office improvement projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage mail through Stable and distribute to appropriate teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track workplace spend, review invoices, and flag cost-saving opportunities with Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support health, safety, and emergency preparedness for the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Operations Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding and offboarding, including HR system workflows, background checks, I-9s, and related communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field People-related questions on onboarding, HR data, benefits, and employment verifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process employee changes in Rippling and partner with IT and Payroll to keep new hire information accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide backup support for time off and time &amp;amp; attendance tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and update People team documentation as processes change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch in on People team projects as they come up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring/ Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience/Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year of experience in office administration, hospitality, or recruiting/human resources setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiting support experience is a huge plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite and Microsoft Office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Recruiting ATS platforms and HRIS tools a plus. (Greenhouse, Ashby, Rippling or Workday for example)&lt;/li&gt;
